# Complete DS chapter revision

This is a complete chapter candidate with a companion appendix, not a replacement of the chapter by the previously reviewed ridge subsection. It preserves the full selected scientific account. No new numerical experiment is part of this task.

## Coverage and selection plan

1. Explain the research question: geometry may reveal relationships with capacity and help select or improve bodies. Establish sampled families briefly before interpreting empirical results.
2. Define ridge measurements and present the stratified association figure, preserving Jörn's explicitly accepted correlation paragraph. Keep the existing model/feature-family comparisons with their actual split distinctions.
3. Explain the product edge/width formula and pentagon identity, alongside square/HKO and sampled rotation counterexamples. Separate a family identity from population association.
4. Retain prospective geometric selection, covariance comparison, generic transfer and tangential-generator transfer. Remove the rejected continuation-criterion aside from narration; retain its methods record.
5. Retain paired height changes, equal-request orientation comparison and adaptive sampling. Put operational coordinate/update details in the appendix.
6. Retain the 448-run matched-start optimizer study, branch-envelope motivation, and endpoint failures. Move precise implementation choices to the existing appendix rather than erase their support.
7. Update the historical baseline with retrospective input recovery, full feature restoration, and partial current-evaluator corroboration. The 91 unresolved targets remain visible. This does not repair separate optimizer or prospective-selection execution histories.
8. Explain that triangle/quadrilateral product groups cannot supply a counterexample by the checked literature result, while their subthreshold comparisons remain informative. No optional new empirical tranche is selected here.

## Output contract

`thesis/candidate/ds-complete-draft/` will contain chapter, appendix, copied figure inputs, bibliography addition and a buildable standalone preview. Source identities and relocation ledger will accompany it. The preview is a review artifact, not a PASS judgment. Existing manuscript labels remain compatible where possible. The parent integrator controls actual thesis selection.

## Pending evidence updates

At intake, current reevaluation succeeded on 14,245 of 14,336 historical bodies; 54 norm-policy and 37 tolerance failures remained under separate repair. Preserve this frozen state unless a checked later handoff supersedes it. No whole-population current certification is inferred.

## Completed candidate and checks

The complete chapter and appendix build to a 19-page standalone PDF. Independent factual review (`factual-review.md`) found two local wording/notation defects, both fixed. The integrator's human-feedback comparison additionally identified early procedural detail, unnecessary digits, ambiguous target terminology and a moved-but-omitted optimizer acceptance rule; these were repaired. The accepted correlation paragraph retains its wording and values except the figure-reference sentence, which now points to two readable panels.

The final opening defines the ridge measurement and presents the observed association before detailed sample counts and sampling law. The original optimizer, adaptation, intervention, transfer and selection content remains. Symplectic ridge area is denoted R consistently; the individual face is F. The previous full chapter is frozen by hash and `chapter.diff` preserves the before/after comparison.

The late revalidation handoff is incorporated: 14,335 capacity intervals, 14,289 accepted scalars, 46 wider intervals, one unresolved body. Historical statistical results are unchanged and are not called independent replication. The appendix retains the initial failures and distinct repair run, so the follow-up does not rewrite historical execution.

All evidence-index paths resolve in an identified main/worktree owner. The final build has no undefined references, citations or overfull boxes. The full first preview was visually inspected as page contact sheets; after enlarging the ridge plots, both final full-page plots and the surrounding prose were inspected at readable resolution. No capacity, feature or model experiment was run. Plotting reads verified historical bytes and retains all 14,336 observations.

## Remaining choices and limitations

- Human review of this complete candidate has not occurred. Its organization is a concrete proposed solution, not evidence of PASS.
- The two ridge figures consume two pages to make all 18 strata readable. This is a deliberate design tradeoff, reversible at integration.
- Models use different held-out splits; the chapter reports their historical results without ranking algorithms against one another. The restored baseline does not certify optimizer trajectories or separate selector populations.
- One historical body still lacks current capacity coverage. This is named in the appendix rather than made a repeated narrative interruption.
- Evidence packets currently live on separate reviewed branches; the integrator must retain them for the relative reproduction paths to work in the assembled repository.
